zcg|n|The twenty-fourth part of a day; sixty minutes. ; The time of the day, as expressed in hours and minutes, and indicated by a timepiece; as, what is the hour? At what hour shall we meet? ; Fixed or appointed time; conjuncture; a particular time or occasion; as, the hour of greatest peril; the man for the hour. ; Certain prayers to be repeated at stated times of the day, as matins and vespers. ; A measure of distance traveled.	a:xaa,55,10~xaa,55,10	n:1ew8,54,6;1iox,45,13~1iox,45,13;1ew8,54,6	N:2a9a,53,6;16jd,36,1;i9y,36,3;1mx4,27,28;1mxh,23,4;2b4n,4,4~1mx4,27,28;2a9a,53,6;1mxh,23,4;2b4n,4,4;i9y,36,3;16jd,36,1
